{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>By the mouth of two witnesses or three witnesses.</b> It is known that two are like a hundred — if so, what is the reason for three witnesses? If we say the two are for testimony and the third for the acceptance of the testimony of the two, there is nothing in the verse's language about acceptance of testimony but only testimony. And the Ramban, z\"l, explained: even though every matter is completed with two witnesses, and even in capital cases, if there were three witnesses there, or four or five or more, they are sent for and they come before us, for through the multiplicity of witnesses the matter is clarified more and the truth becomes known to us; but when there were only two witnesses there, or they were there but had already gone away, these two who are present with us suffice — and this is 'by the mouth of two witnesses,' if there were no more, 'or three witnesses' if they were found there, and the same applies to four and five. And the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded: 'By the mouth of two witnesses or three witnesses' — if testimony is established by two, why did the verse specify three? Rather, to juxtapose three to two: just as two are one testimony, so three are one testimony, and the same holds for a hundred — to exclude a relative or disqualified witness, whose testimony of all of them is void if one of them was a relative or disqualified, since testimony of which part is voided is entirely voided, when all of them gathered to testify." "<b>And they said</b> in the Midrash: 'Or three witnesses' — the verse added the third to teach you that even if all three testified falsely, the third too is punished with the punishment of the two, so that you should not say the third carries no consequence since the testimony is established by those two whether for liability or for exemption. And the verse teaches you that everyone who attaches himself to transgressors is punished like the transgressors. And from here Rabbi Akiva would prove the giving of reward to the righteous: if the one who attaches himself to transgressors is punished like the committers of transgression, all the more so the one who attaches himself to those who fulfill commandments — they give him reward like those who fulfill commandments, for the measure of goodness is multiplied over the measure of punishment by one to five hundred, as it is said (Exodus 34:7) ״נוצר חסד לאלפים״ and it is written (ibid.) ״פוקד עון אבות על בנים ועל בני בנים על שלשים ועל רבעים״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "The verse citation (Exodus 34:7) reads שלשים ועל רבעים — literally 'to the third and fourth generation' — where the standard text has שלשים ועל רבעים; Rabbeinu Bahya writes שלשים ועל רבעים, preserved as in his text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:04.077257042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}